    {
      "id": "claim_c759e685a80a401a91d950b98c680556",
      "statement": "The app has exactly six App Router pages (/, /login, /catalog, /changelog, /army/[id], /army/[id]/edit), all declared 'use client'; there is no middleware.ts, so access control is per-page: only the dashboard gates on user (skeleton while isLoading, then renders LoginPage inline when !user) and /login redirects to / via router.replace once a user exists, while /catalog, /changelog and both army routes render for anonymous visitors on the API client's localStorage fallbacks.",
